WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:02.980
- [Narrator] These are the three
top-selling oat milk brands

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:04.310
in the US.

00:00:04.310 --> 00:00:07.340
But this is probably the one
you're most familiar with.

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:08.970
That's because a few years ago,

00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:11.140
Oatly overhauled its marketing strategy,

00:00:11.140 --> 00:00:13.030
taking its products from Sweden

00:00:13.030 --> 00:00:15.120
to grocery stores around the world,

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:16.660
including the US.

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:18.720
- Before Oatly expanded in the US,

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:21.450
oat milk was relatively
unknown to the US consumer.

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:24.120
It was really Oatly that
started the oat milk category

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:25.070
in the US.

00:00:25.070 --> 00:00:26.660
- [Narrator] But the
company has a problem.

00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:28.530
Just look at their stock price.

00:00:28.530 --> 00:00:30.640
It dropped in part because
Oatly can't keep up

00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:32.110
with the demand for oat milk,

00:00:32.110 --> 00:00:34.330
demand that it largely created.

00:00:34.330 --> 00:00:36.960
Here's why Oatly, a
one-time Wall Street darling

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:39.110
that brought oat milk
to the American stage

00:00:39.110 --> 00:00:41.153
has lost market share to rivals.

00:00:41.153 --> 00:00:43.050
(dramatic music)

00:00:43.050 --> 00:00:45.170
Let's rewind to 2019

00:00:45.170 --> 00:00:47.420
when demand for Oatly was rising thanks

00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:48.870
to quirky advertisement

00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:51.640
and placement in independent coffee shops.

00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:53.170
CEO Toni Petersson

00:00:53.170 --> 00:00:55.200
had brought his long-time
friend John Schoolcraft

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:57.560
to Oatly to build a creative department.

00:00:57.560 --> 00:00:58.790
- And we came up with this line.

00:00:58.790 --> 00:01:01.600
It's like milk, but made for humans.

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:02.540
Very simple.

00:01:02.540 --> 00:01:03.670
- [Narrator] He created a team,

00:01:03.670 --> 00:01:06.240
which jokingly calls
itself the Oatly Department

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:07.350
of Mind Control.

00:01:07.350 --> 00:01:09.477
And rebranded with slogans like.

00:01:09.477 --> 00:01:12.430
♪ Wow no cow ♪

00:01:12.430 --> 00:01:15.360
- [Narrator] But that wasn't
the only tactic Oatly used.

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:16.930
- Oatly developed relationships

00:01:16.930 --> 00:01:19.890
with baristas in independent
and third-wave coffee shops

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:21.830
and it really became interesting, cool

00:01:21.830 --> 00:01:23.920
and alternative amongst this niche market.

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:25.820
And then the baristas
started talking about it

00:01:25.820 --> 00:01:26.900
on social media.

00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:28.770
- [Narrator] And as one of
the only oat milk producers

00:01:28.770 --> 00:01:31.040
on the market, they helped create a craze.

00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:33.740
Since 2019, the oat milk market in the US

00:01:33.740 --> 00:01:36.770
has grown by roughly 330%.

00:01:36.770 --> 00:01:38.490
To maintain their buzzy status,

00:01:38.490 --> 00:01:40.960
Oatly needed to be able
to produce enough oat milk

00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:42.740
to actually meet that demand,

00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:44.570
and that was becoming a problem.

00:01:44.570 --> 00:01:47.240
At first, Oatly had relied on contractors,

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:48.770
which was expensive compared

00:01:48.770 --> 00:01:50.350
to making it themselves.

00:01:50.350 --> 00:01:52.630
So Oatly built its first US factory

00:01:52.630 --> 00:01:54.200
in Millville, New Jersey

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:56.350
but it didn't go as planned.

00:01:56.350 --> 00:01:58.020
- Production at the
Millville plant started

00:01:58.020 --> 00:01:59.760
about six months behind target

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:01.690
and it was hampered by poor planning.

00:02:01.690 --> 00:02:03.120
There was wastewater issues,

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:04.890
as well as equipment malfunctioning.

00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:06.330
- [Narrator] An Oatly spokeswoman said

00:02:06.330 --> 00:02:08.130
there was no wastewater treatment system

00:02:08.130 --> 00:02:09.570
initially planned for Millville,

00:02:09.570 --> 00:02:12.080
and that one was added in August 2021.

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:13.810
All wastewater from the new facility

00:02:13.810 --> 00:02:16.370
has been within permit range, she said.

00:02:16.370 --> 00:02:18.300
She added that it is best practice

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:19.740
to scale production quickly

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:21.340
to resolve technical issues

00:02:21.340 --> 00:02:23.230
and the approach didn't cause delays,

00:02:23.230 --> 00:02:25.640
affect output or increase cost.

00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:27.360
She said that "By any metric,

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:30.530
our Millville facility is
best-in-class in construction,

00:02:30.530 --> 00:02:33.470
execution, safety and quality."

00:02:33.470 --> 00:02:36.830
In late 2018, Oatly had
purchased a second factory

00:02:36.830 --> 00:02:40.190
in Ogden, Utah but it
didn't solve their problems.

00:02:40.190 --> 00:02:42.500
And in fact, it created more.

00:02:42.500 --> 00:02:43.800
- At the Ogden, Utah plant,

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:45.280
there was two major problems.

00:02:45.280 --> 00:02:47.230
One, they spent more than they intended.

00:02:47.230 --> 00:02:49.280
They had hoped to spend 50 million

00:02:49.280 --> 00:02:50.980
and they spent over 100 million,

00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:53.130
and then second, they
didn't finish on time.

00:02:53.130 --> 00:02:55.410
They had hoped to finish by early 2020

00:02:55.410 --> 00:02:57.220
and took way longer than that.

00:02:57.220 --> 00:02:58.340
- [Narrator] An Oatly spokeswoman

00:02:58.340 --> 00:03:00.760
said the executives
frequently updated the board

00:03:00.760 --> 00:03:02.060
on changes to the budget,

00:03:02.060 --> 00:03:03.810
adding that the budget was in line

00:03:03.810 --> 00:03:05.430
with other modern facilities.

00:03:05.430 --> 00:03:06.690
She also said that many

00:03:06.690 --> 00:03:08.570
of the challenges at the Ogden facility

00:03:08.570 --> 00:03:10.410
have been compounded by the pandemic.

00:03:10.410 --> 00:03:13.420
But the company has made
continuous improvements.

00:03:13.420 --> 00:03:17.160
In 2021, Oatly's market
share in the US was 26%

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:18.380
of retail sales.

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:21.230
That's a decrease of 6% from 2019.

00:03:21.230 --> 00:03:23.440
And stock prices have followed suit.

00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:26.600
Meanwhile, competitors saw
demand for oat milk grow

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:28.370
and shortages of Oatly allowed them

00:03:28.370 --> 00:03:30.830
to swoop in and snag market share.

00:03:30.830 --> 00:03:33.660
Dairy giant HP Hood launched Planet Oat,

00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:36.240
which Hood says sells for 1 to $2 less

00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:38.020
than competing brands.

00:03:38.020 --> 00:03:40.540
Planet Oat overtook Oatly in 2021

00:03:40.540 --> 00:03:43.100
and now leads the US retail market.

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:45.000
Another dairy company, Chobani,

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:47.400
made their first venture
into plant-based products

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:49.700
with oat milk in late 2019.

00:03:49.700 --> 00:03:52.190
Chobani said they constructed
a plant within a plant

00:03:52.190 --> 00:03:54.770
and that the construction
took them less than 12 months

00:03:54.770 --> 00:03:56.430
and allowed for far more capacity

00:03:56.430 --> 00:03:58.750
than there was demand at the time.

00:03:58.750 --> 00:04:01.860
Now Chobani holds third
place in US retail sales

00:04:01.860 --> 00:04:03.900
after Planet Oat and Oatly.

00:04:03.900 --> 00:04:06.220
- Competitors such as Hood and Chobani

00:04:06.220 --> 00:04:07.920
really raced to jump in this market

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:09.410
when Oatly was having troubles

00:04:09.410 --> 00:04:11.520
and they capitalized on Oatly's struggles.

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:14.480
- [Narrator] Plus, Oatly's
stock has fallen about 80%

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:17.760
since its IPO in May 2021.

00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:19.550
That summer, the board was considering

00:04:19.550 --> 00:04:20.990
a successor to Petersson.

00:04:20.990 --> 00:04:22.690
They specifically wanted a candidate

00:04:22.690 --> 00:04:24.440
with more operational experience,

00:04:24.440 --> 00:04:27.230
so Petersson could devote his
time to business development,

00:04:27.230 --> 00:04:29.200
people familiar with the matter said.

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:32.150
In April, Oatly hired a
former senior executive

00:04:32.150 --> 00:04:34.910
at candy giant Mars, Inc as president.

00:04:34.910 --> 00:04:36.650
Oatly's chairman said in a statement

00:04:36.650 --> 00:04:39.220
that the hire was part of the
board's succession planning

00:04:39.220 --> 00:04:40.070
and that the company

00:04:40.070 --> 00:04:42.710
is not considering a transition right now.

00:04:42.710 --> 00:04:44.740
- Operational experience is very important

00:04:44.740 --> 00:04:47.820
because Oatly is trying to
expand its manufacturing capacity

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:49.340
and it's having production issues,

00:04:49.340 --> 00:04:51.810
and a lot of that stems
from operational issues.

00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:53.540
- [Narrator] Whoever
leads Oatly going forward

00:04:53.540 --> 00:04:54.980
will face challenges.

00:04:54.980 --> 00:04:57.320
In May, global production output decreased

00:04:57.320 --> 00:04:59.060
in the fourth quarter of 2021

00:04:59.060 --> 00:05:02.400
with the company citing
pandemic-related factors.

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:05.540
Oatly's stock hit a
low of under $3 in May,

00:05:05.540 --> 00:05:08.470
reflecting difficulties it
has had with production.

00:05:08.470 --> 00:05:10.720
- The primary challenge
that a new CEO will face

00:05:10.720 --> 00:05:12.260
has to do with the manufacturing

00:05:12.260 --> 00:05:14.350
and ensuring that supply meets demand.

00:05:14.350 --> 00:05:15.240
- [Narrator] In the meantime,

00:05:15.240 --> 00:05:17.884
the oat milk market will
continue to be contested.

00:05:17.884 --> 00:05:20.467
(lively music)

